It is evening.
Now the rain has stopped and a nice breeze is blowing.
I am standing at the bus stop.
That red BEST bus arrives.
I get on the bus.
"Brother, give me one ticket," I tell the conductor.
He gives me a ticket.
I find a window seat and sit down.
I look outside.
These streets have become wet and shiny from the rain.
I remember my first bus journey.
That journey happened five months ago.
At that time, I was feeling very nervous.
This bus, these people, this city... everything was new.
But today it doesn't feel like that.
Today I feel very calm and settled.
This city feels like my own to me now.
This commute and this life in Mumbai are familiar to me now.
